@startuml
title Figure 11 — Concentric delivery rings
skinparam linetype polyline
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

circle "R5\nHardening + demo" as R5 {
  circle "R4\nGrounded provider path" as R4 {
    circle "R3\nDeterministic analysis + history" as R3 {
      circle "R2\nRelational read slice" as R2 {
        circle "R1\nAuthenticated synthetic read slice" as R1 {
          circle "R0\nDeployable hollow shell" as R0
        }
      }
    }
  }
}

legend right
  |= Ring |= Activation |
  | R0 | Java/Spring/React shell, project-owned contracts and ports |
  | R1 | Authenticated synthetic customer/activity/risk read slice |
  | R2 | JPA/PostgreSQL/Flyway/Testcontainers behind CustomerActivityPort |
  | R3 | Static grounding, deterministic analysis, persistent reviewable history |
  | R4 | pgvector retrieval and optional live AI provider adapter |
  | R5 | Reliability, observability and demo hardening |
endlegend

note bottom of R5
  Each outer ring extends the same architecture by replacing or activating adapters.
  It does not create a parallel throwaway architecture.
end note
@enduml
